# Instrument 4-11 — the waystation on the north road.
#
# The four things entry 030 says a mission needs that a map deliberately cannot hold, plus the
# squads and what ours are told about theirs. This file replaced three copies of the same facts — a prose header in
# content/maps/waystation.hexmap, a scenario in game/scripts/SandboxScenario.cs, and a harness in
# content/Hexcom.Content.Tests/Waystation. Entry 038 said what was wrong with three; entry 047
# says what this is instead, and entry 052 removed the last of them. Anything that wants to fight
# the waystation reads this.
#
# The task is a look, so the register is the mission book's assessment rather than its walk, and
# the objective it wants is reconnaissance. Entry 059 wrote everything but that line and entry 061
# built the rule under it; it runs now, and the walk-out this file used to state is gone.

mission Instrument 4-11: the waystation
map waystation

# ---- the briefing, in the mission book's six parts ------------------------------------------
#
# Written in the words the squad is given, which is why it names posts and not people: the
# Commission does not know that the man outside the west gate is called Cobb. The deployments
# below know, because a readout has to call him something. Entry 046.

brief instrument  Instrument 4-11 continues in force and this is an inspection of the waystation
brief instrument  on the north road, filed accordingly. Nobody is at war and you are a
brief instrument  maintenance visit.

brief presence    A detail of four, we think, and the last two reports disagree about the fourth.
brief presence    One stands on the road outside the west gate, twenty-five metres out, watching
brief presence    the way anybody sensible would come. One is on the roof of the house inside the
brief presence    compound and that is the one with the set, so whatever he works out, all of
brief presence    them know. A rifle in the tower to the south-east, four metres up, too far from
brief presence    the west road to notice what he could hit. One more in the barn on the east
brief presence    road, who hears nothing the roof does not tell him. They are a fortnight into a
brief presence    rotation and they are bored, which is the whole of your advantage.

brief task        Get eyes on what is stored in the house inside the compound, properly on it,
brief task        and come out with the answer.

brief restraint   You will not be seen and you will not fire. If the shift sees you the task is
brief restraint   over and you will still not fire. The people in the cottages are not part of
brief restraint   this and they live here.

brief way-off     Off by the cottages, west of the stream and north of the road, before first
brief way-off     light. Not the road you came in by: the man at the gate has had all night to
brief way-off     watch it, and nobody is coming to get you.

brief stop        If one of them properly registers you and lives to keep it, or has already
brief stop        passed it to the roof, the answer is worth nothing before you are home. Come
brief stop        back by the cottages. There is nothing here worth the second half of the night.

# ---- named ground ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# What the briefing says out loud, so the objective can refer to it and the view can label it.
#
# The house is the thing to look at and it is sealed: of the 1693 places a soldier can stand
# outside the wall, not one has a line into it. Of the 54 inside, fourteen do, all of them south
# of the door and all fourteen overlooked by the roof. The drain under the south wall opens at
# -1,-3, which is one of the fourteen. So the ground already says what the mission is — in by the
# drain, the look from where you land, and the man on the roof is the whole problem. Measured,
# and held by a test in the harness.

place cottages hexes -14,6 -14,7 -13,6
place compound disc 0,0 r 4
place house disc 0,1 r 1

# ---- who is standing where ------------------------------------------------------------------

# Ours, on the west road about twenty hexes out, facing the crossroads. Twenty hexes is 35 m at
# the 1.73 m pitch entry 007 fixed, which is far enough out that the distances discriminate.
deploy Vance  player -21,3  facing se role scout   kit infiltrator
deploy Orsini player -20,0  facing ne role trooper kit heavy
deploy Bekker player -19,-3 facing ne              kit rifleman

# Theirs, out of docs/setting/roster.md section 5 — the Cadre detail that holds this stretch of
# road. Cobb has the gate, Teague has the roof and the set, Marek is in the tower and Hollis is in
# the barn. AwarenessTracker.CanReach gives a radio the whole side, so whatever Teague works out,
# the tower and the barn know and neither could have seen it. Both of them are outside earshot of
# the compound (entry 037), so if the roof goes quiet, so do they.
deploy Cobb   hostile -5,0     facing sw                 kit beamer
deploy Teague hostile 0,1@1    facing nw role signaller  kit beamer
deploy Marek  hostile 16,-14@1 facing nw                 kit rifleman
deploy Hollis hostile 14,-6    facing sw                 kit beamer

# ---- what the squad is told -----------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The presence part of the briefing, as the rules hold it: a marker on each post in every contact
# file on our side before the first turn. Without these the squad walks its first turn blind down
# the road the gate watches, because at the start of Vance's turn nobody has looked yet and there
# is nothing registered to keep out of the eye of. Entry 087 measured that, and fought the same
# seeds with all four posts told at Searching to see what a squad that had read its briefing does.
#
# The file says less than that arm did, because the briefing does. Three posts are stated flat —
# the gate, the roof, the tower — and Searching is the rung a soldier will go and check. The barn
# is "one more", after "the last two reports disagree about the fourth", so it is told at
# Suspicious: somebody there, probably, and nobody would stake a route on it.
told player searching  Cobb Teague Marek
told player suspicious Hollis

# ---- what we came to do ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# In to look at the house, out by the cottages, and nobody the wiser. Reconnaissance is won by
# holding the place in full attention with a clear line to it and then getting off the ground —
# SightSolver.Trace and AwarenessTracker.IsWatching, two calls that already existed, plus the
# objective entry 061 built around them. See docs/setting/missions.md section 4.
#
# This line used to be a comment beside a withdrawal, because the rules had only the leaving and
# the leaving alone is achieved by turning round and going home: twelve matches out of twelve did
# exactly that in round 2, which is entry 048. There is something in the middle of it now.
#
# 'at house' is the seven hexes named above and the look is aimed at the middle of them, which is
# the room rather than the doorway. How close it has to be taken from is left to the rule — twelve
# metres — because the house is only seen into from inside the yard anyway, and a distance written
# here as well as there is a number with two homes.
#
# Suspicious is a dog barking at 25; Searching is 50, the rung where a sentry stops scanning and
# starts walking towards where he thinks you were. The brief says properly registered, so a
# suspicion is survivable.
objective reconnaissance player at house exit cottages unnoticed suspicious

# Before first light. Thirty rounds covers every fight seen on this ground with room to spare —
# entry 038 measured the fighting over by round 21. Since entry 082 a rule reads it: it is the
# deadline on the objective above, and a squad still on the field after round 30 has abandoned
# the mission rather than failed it.
#
# The briefing's stop — "or has already passed it to the roof" — is the alarm, and the format can
# now say how long the mission outlives it with 'rounds 30 after-alarm N'. It says nothing yet on
# purpose. Entry 083 and 087 measured three rounds and called it harsh for this ground and the
# playtest's to set, and a figure written here would be the first thing anybody took for settled.
rounds 30
